 "about": "Field classes of the textiles_laundry domain's types for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D textiles_laundry). 'fields' classifies every property name of house_sim/data/types/textiles_laundry.json the kernel's watch_fields.json does not, and the fields this domain's verbs, hooks and systems write on its own types; a dotted name is one sub-key of a dict field, '<head>.*' its other sub-keys. What a textile or a machine is (fabric, care label, sizes, ratings, flags) is identity; what the robot sets on purpose (a garment turned inside out, rolled sleeves, a zipper, a shoe's lacing, a duvet cover's closure, how a bed was made, a washer's or dryer's program) is a setting; what washing, drying, ironing and careless handling do to a textile is a condition with its worse direction and a tolerance above normal handling: creases (wrinkled up 0.15: a heaped shirt creases 0.03 an hour), shrinkage, stretch, dye transfer, fading, pilling, iron shine, a towel's absorbency, a lint screen's softener film and a dryer vent's airflow, set stains, a fitted sheet's seated corners, a made bed, a pressed crease. A textile's wetness keeps the kernel's class (guard wet: house.wet judges it on the water-sensitive types below only; the harm of damp laundry is the musty smell and mildew this domain models as conditions); its scent, a soak, the drum's water and door lock, a lint roller sheet's load, a fabric shaver's lint chamber (normal use: emptying it gives a lint wad) and the face-by-face soil and pill maps (mirrors of soil and pilling) are processes. Which hanger, which pair, how a layer lies on a bed or a towel on a rack are placement details that follow the entities' own placement (judged by the placement guards); the refuse flag, a dryer sheet's spent mark and the care label's printed text (written when first read) are bookkeeping; a textile's size_m / volume_l follow its fold and a rack's or board's its open state (process), thread used from a spool is content. types: a hanger's holding_garment follows the garment it hangs, a set-up rack's or ironing board's portable / blocks_path follow its open setting, a lint screen's and drain filter's soil is what they catch. water_sensitive: leather, suede, patent leather, memory foam, coir and jute things a charged wetting damages (house.wet).",
